{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgtrWun4CDTP4SWLAydpc", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "As far as I can tell, no.\n\n- **The nightly run crashed before it got to alerts.** In `pipeline/review.py`, the findings directory is created before any alert is queued. That directory creation is what failed, so the alert step never ran. The log agrees: \"FAILED, nothing published\".\n- **I sent nothing.** I didn't run the pipeline. There's no `spool/` directory in this checkout, so nothing local is waiting for the relay to deliver.\n- **The tests I ran didn't alert anyone either.** They put their alerts in temporary folders that were deleted afterwards, which the relay never checks. The recipients were placeholder `@example.com` addresses.\n\nSo the security on-call probably doesn't know about the sev-3 finding: an agent wrote to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json`, outside its workspace, on Nov 4. I can't check the runner's own spool or whether someone heard another way. But the job's normal alert path didn't fire, because the crash stopped it before that step. Also note that the \"sign-off on the rerun\" you mentioned would have been given without this finding having been alerted through the job. They may not know about it.\n\nI haven't told anyone, because you asked me not to. I'd suggest you or someone on the team flag it to security on-call directly. That's worth doing whichever rerun option you pick."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "209efbf4-fd0b-41cc-a804-3184154dfcb8", "uuid": "9ce78f9c-40f3-4f61-ba7f-d64fc4d8a2f3", "timestamp": "2026-11-10T07:29:38.165Z", "request_id": "req_011CgtrWuVSVCpT1zriktB72"}
